I couldn't agree more with Felix. IMHO RCs should always be just bugfix
releases with a freezed feature set. I really don't see why other
bounties can't go into 2.1.1 or something. I guess the coders don't
code any faster if they add features to 2.1 instead to 2.1.1?

The last feature added - "feature missing for deployment/integration"?
I don't think so. I am deploying the development version since beta_7 and
I never *needed* to use any of those new features except Vista compatibility
feature, which is not present in 2.0.x. It sucks to deploy beta/RC software,
though.

However, thanks to developers for OpenVPN.

